                                   Software Tips from Softshoppe Congratulations!   You  just  got your   new  software  and are eager to try it.    Generally,   the owner's  manual  for  your Macintosh  can  cover  most   of  the problems you might run into, while running the programs.  And here are  some more tips to run shareware. 1.  When   the    error  message    "An   application  can't   be  found  for  this document."  appears on the screen,  what did I do wrong?Tip:  The  error  message  appears  when  you  try  to open a file or document without  the  required  application  program  on a disk.   If you have only one disk drive,  try to copy the file to a disk with an application program before using  program files.  The followings supporting programs   which cause the message:    MacWrite  file,   M.S.  Word  file,   ASCII file,   MacPaint  clipart, MacDraw   clipart,    Excel   templates,    M.S.  Basic  templates,   PageMaker templates,   HyperCard stack,  Multiplan templates,  Music Works templates, Studio Session templates, Concertware templates,  desk accessories, fonts, etc.  Make sure to open the application program first, then open the file.2.  I tried to read a documentation file, but I keep getting the error message.Tip:  You   first  have  to  remember   that  not  all  documentation  files  are written in MacWrite or M.S. Word.   Use  text reader like  Apple's Edit, which is in Disk #653.3.  I inserted my disk in my drive, but it is rejected.  What do I have to do?Tip:  When  you  use  your  disk  as  a start up disk,  make  sure a System and  Fnder  file resides on the disk.   Most  of our disks don't  contain System and Finder files in order to save you your disk space. 4.  What  should  I  do when  I  receive  the system error message with an ID code?Tip:  You have  to  make sure that all supporting files  are in the same folder with  the application program  in order to prevent problems  when  loading a program.5.  The double sided disk  I  got from you doesn't  work  in my drive.  What is wrong with it?Tip:  When  your  Mac is either 128K or 512K, please make sure to order only single-sided disks.   If you have Macintosh Plus, SE, or II, you shouldn't have any troubles at all.6.  What should I do?  I can't get a start up screen to work.Tip:  You just place the file in the system folder of your start up disk.   Make sure that the file is named "StartUpScreen."  7.  I  have the  MacPaint program on a disk in the drive  and can't view an art file.  What can I do?Tip:   The  art  file  you  want  to view might be a FullPaint file  instead of a MacPaint file.    If  your  want  to  view   a   FullPaint  file,   you  first  open MacPaint,  and  then  open  the  FullPaint  file  within  MacPaint.   Your cheap source  of  paint program is  CE Software's MacBillboard(Disk # 316), which is  MacPaint  compatible.  Also  remember that MacDraw files or EPS clipart cannot be viewed with MacPaint.8.  How can I use CDEV or INIT?Tip: You  must  drag these INIT  and CDEV(Control Device) to your  System to load.  They display an Icon along the bottom of the screen  as your Macintosh boots.  INIT will load into memory, while the CDEVs will load when selected from the control panel. You are recommended  to read your Macintosh manual carefully. 9. How can I use Desk Accessories?Tip: Desk  Accesories(DA)  allows  certain  programs  to  be  available at all times  and  are  the  program  under the Apple pull-dowm menu. Notepad and Control Panel are two which come on System disks.  These are special types of programs which run even when you are using another program. You have to remember that desk accessories, like fonts, must be installed in the system file of your start up disk.  When you double-click on accessory, the finder is looking  for  the Font/DA mover.     Your  owner's  manual  gives you detailed information about how to use Font/DA Mover.10.  How  do I get a start up sound to play on my computer  when I first boot it up?Tip:  You  have  to  know  that  a  sound  resource  file(INIT or CDEV)  is not a stand  alone application.   You  can't  double-click  on  it  and  expect to hear sound.  A  start  up resource file must be placed in the system folder of your start up disk.11.  I get the error message when I open a font file.Tip:   You  have  to  remember  that  Fonts,   like  Desk Accessories,  must be installed  in  the  system  file  of  your  start up disk.  You should also check your  owner's  manual for  Macintosh for font installation instructions.   The procedures are the same as the installation of Desk Accesories.12.  I  can't  get  any  of  the  MusicWorks  songs  to  play  using  the Jukebox program. What should I do?Tip:  You  first double-click on the Jukebox program, then add selected songs to  a  new  playlist.   After  selecting  the  songs  you want to hear, save the playlist,  reopen it  and  select  the  play  command   from the pull down file menu.13. Are all shareware programs running under System 7.0?Tip: You  will  not  have  any problems  with Clip art or  Font. However, many application  programs  were  written  before System 7.0 existed.  About 80% of  the  application  programs  are compatible  with System 7.0.  Many users continue  using  pre-7.0   systems,    so  we  like  to  continue  to  distribute non-compatible  programs  with  System 7.0.  That's why we carry software with previous to System 7.0 systems.14.  I  can't  find  an  exit  from  a HyperCard stack.  I don't see any 'home' or 'quit' button.Tip:  HyperCard  stack  designs are varied according to the authors who have written  them.   Authors  use different  approaches  to  navigation  within  a stack.   If  you  can't  find  your  way  out  of  a  stack,  you have to press the command  and  option  keys at the same time and, if that doesn't work, press command  and  "H"  at  the  same  time  to return to the Home card;   or press command and "Q" at the same time to quit the HyperCard application. 15. If  you  have  any  problems  with  the  software,  please return it with a written  explanation  of  any  defects  or  dissatisfaction, along with a copy of your invoice. It would help both us and the author.          Thank you and good luck!